course: dictionary
lesson: 15486
title: Striving: trying very hard
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Striving means trying very hard for a long time to get or reach something. Look at the words around it. It is often followed by "for" or "to". «She is striving to improve her spelling.» The words "to improve" tell you what she wants, and the idea of working hard is the feeling inside striving.
explain: Striving can also be a noun, meaning the effort itself. «Her striving paid off when she won the race.» Here striving means all the hard effort she put in. To check, swap in "hard effort" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: You will often hear striving in school mottos and assemblies, like «striving for excellence» or «always striving to do our best». The clue is that the effort goes on over time. Striving is not a quick try, but steady hard work towards a goal.
fact: Striving means trying very hard for a long time to get or reach something.
fact: «Striving» is often followed by «for» or «to», as in «striving for» and «striving to».
fact: As a noun, striving means the effort of trying hard, or the things a person tries hard for.
fact: «She is striving to improve her spelling» means she is working hard, over time, to get better at spelling.
fact: Striving is about effort that continues, so one quick try is not really striving.
exercise: «The team is striving to win the cup.» What does striving mean here? | Giving up quickly | Sleeping soundly | *Trying very hard over a long time | Laughing loudly
exercise: «He is striving for excellence in every subject.» What is he trying hard to get? | Sleep | *Excellence | Lunch | Rain
exercise: «Her striving paid off when she won the race.» Here striving is a noun. What does it mean? | A small prize | A fast car | *Hard effort | A loud noise
test: «Our class is always striving to do our best.» What does this tell you? | Being bored | *Working hard over time to do well | Doing the least possible | Forgetting the work
test: «The school motto is "striving for excellence".» What does "for excellence" show? | The time school finishes | The colour of the uniform | *What the school is trying hard to reach | The name of the school hall
exam: «The explorers kept striving towards the far mountains through the deep snow.» What does striving towards a goal suggest? | Stopping to sleep | Walking slowly to rest | Getting lost on purpose | *Working hard against difficulties to reach a goal
